{"id": "EUVD-2026-81717", "enisaUuid": "054677b1-0e2f-3221-9d9b-75aa990a007b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nirqchip/renesas-rzg2l: Fix loss of interrupt\n\nrzg2l_clear_irq_int() and rzg2l_clear_tint_int() perform a\nread-modify-write on the ISCR/TSCR status registers to clear the bit\nfor the interrupt just handled. Since these registers are\nwrite-0-to-clear per bit, this is racy:\n\nIf another interrupt's status bit gets set between the read and the write,\nthat bit is written back as 0 by the software-constructed value, clearing\nan interrupt that hasn't been serviced yet and losing it.\n\nThis can be reproduced by triggering multiple interrupts at once, e.g.:\n\n  gpioset -c gpiochip0 355=0 353=0 328=0 352=0\n\nFix this by writing back only the bit being cleared, with all other bits\nset to 1, instead of read-modify-writing the whole register.  Since 1-bits\nare left unchanged by hardware, concurrently-set status bits for other\ninterrupts are preserved.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:58:22", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c043591f03a8111f7d306b8122c444a949486269", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5ba8b861b5d833394bd23df3f4b59883ef18c88", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3791e242ec2e5a5cd9e010a75ed1125d0e84d394", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/38c6831fefde0ff89f8d2dcb924f957a89dec414", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dbecbe23dc606c4af68b4591a41124186f5c1802", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50b10bd0c2d721ad38abd1abe3acdefb6caa0944"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h8c5-9rgx-f76h", "CVE-2026-90124"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2384483d-8b9b-3446-abc3-b651db1a8063", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3fed09559cd8be79568d368ce02bf7f2d56259b6 <3791e242ec2e5a5cd9e010a75ed1125d0e84d394"}, {"id": "2696050d-a782-3837-a81c-e957965bf0f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3fed09559cd8be79568d368ce02bf7f2d56259b6 <b5ba8b861b5d833394bd23df3f4b59883ef18c88"}, {"id": "5e86c314-5af9-3ccf-b102-c97186c746c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3fed09559cd8be79568d368ce02bf7f2d56259b6 <38c6831fefde0ff89f8d2dcb924f957a89dec414"}, {"id": "605b83b5-3bb7-3167-a241-5ba12d8c5f98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "76599ce3-fcea-345f-9f64-85d096d120c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "8a244bc1-fef9-39c9-831b-a8378d9647ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3fed09559cd8be79568d368ce02bf7f2d56259b6 <dbecbe23dc606c4af68b4591a41124186f5c1802"}, {"id": "9392fde1-80cd-37dd-9aa0-f6ba34210b97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9dfde0d2-b008-3cb9-b378-8d6e07ed8032", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "a02aedb5-b501-3176-b573-57a6b3d4c3e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3fed09559cd8be79568d368ce02bf7f2d56259b6 <50b10bd0c2d721ad38abd1abe3acdefb6caa0944"}, {"id": "bc1f3a49-cd97-32a2-86a1-5db43dc8e71c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "db1dce5c-3145-3dab-a8b0-526cda500037", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "ea854377-866d-3f18-83be-d7566d419960", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3fed09559cd8be79568d368ce02bf7f2d56259b6 <c043591f03a8111f7d306b8122c444a949486269"}, {"id": "eab70696-851b-34db-98a2-364293b27d41", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "f4ee523d-f5ee-3672-b977-a